Z||000000||count_iblis||11-12-2000||06:01 PM||||OK, I have considered my options,  I found a 3.1 engine for 200.00 and my mechaninc said he would install it for me for 400.00 (due to he is a long time fiero fanantic like us and he thinks that it will be fun).  But he wants me to find some information about so he dosent mess up anyhting.  Can you guys and gals help point me in the direction where i can find not a step by step operation but just some of the important details that we are going to have to know about.  If anyone has doen this could you send some picuters of the project if you have any.  my email is chrisbarger@kvnet.org<P><BR>Thanks, <P>Chris<P>------------------<BR>COUNTIBLIS <BR>"HUG YOUR KIDS SPANK THE SOUND BARRIER"||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||11-12-2000||08:19 PM||||Count, <BR>You didn't mention which heads this engine has, or what kind of vehicle it came from.<BR>If it came from a minivan (only), I believe it's got the cast iron heads. Should be a fairly straightforward replacement. If it came from a car, it probably has GEN II aluminum heads, and the Fiero intake system won't bolt up. This will normally prevent the Fiero distributor from being installed, due to the placement of the throttle body.  There might have been a Z-24 with aluminum  heads <I>and</I> a distributor. If so, that would be the intake manifold to use. Most of the aluminum head motors were DIS, though. If you want to use the DIS, then you'll have to change ECM's, and do some wiring. <BR>Others have been down this road, before. Maybe someone else can add to/correct what I've posted.<P>Raydar<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ghia||11-14-2000||12:17 AM||||Count,<P>Why would you want to do this?  Why don't you do what I did.  I took my stock 2.8 and put in a bigger crank and pistons and a cam so I wouldn't have to worry about rewiring or other compatibility issues and I have a very reliable 3.1.  ||||reg||5
